  "caveats": [
    "Purely algebraic O_q(SU(2)) / U_q(sl_2) representation theory delivers an exact, zero-parameter non-tracial modular state (p_+/p_- = q_0^2) and exact Blanco-Casini-Hung-Myers entanglement first law S(sigma) - S(rho) + D(sigma || rho) = Tr((sigma - rho) K_rho), plus three distinct boundary regimes: (E1/E3a) local U_q(sl_2) cup punctures giving S/N_Sigma = s_Haar(q_0) = 0.6877331765..., (E2) direct J=0 singlet projection where q_0^{2 J_z} = 1 collapses rho_Sigma|_{sing} to (1/C_m) I_{C_m} with q-independent S = ln C_m -> N_Sigma ln 2, and (E3b) half-system trace of a 2*N_Sigma global singlet which retains genuine finite-N_Sigma q_0-splitting with UV-regulated spin-j magnetic edge saturation S_inf^{edge}(q_0) = 2.56875892... while also converging to ln 2 per strand. However, every un-tuned algebraic area candidate (1, 3/4, sqrt(3)/2, C_2^{(q_0)}(1/2), sqrt(C_2^{(q_0)}(1/2)), [2]_{q_0}^2, and gamma_BI=1 8*pi*sqrt(C_2^{(q_0)})) misses 1/4 = 0.25 by >= 30.9%, confirming Option 4A (`dc9894be61b`) that the numerical factor 1/4 = (2*pi)/(8*pi) strictly requires the continuum 4D Lorentzian Bisognano-Wichmann / Einstein-Raychaudhuri geometric bridge (`HaarLorentzianModularBridgeConjecture`)."
